margins":-0.12368251099679586,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.011547940104516576,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.4327793648938878,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":65.47619047619048,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.054180004,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":36.1,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Entera Bio Ltd., a clinical stage company, engages in the development of oral peptides and protein replacement therapies in Israel and internationally. It develops EB613, an oral teriparatide, which completed the Phase II clinical trial for the treatment of osteoporosis and Phase I clinical trial for the treatment of stress fractures. The company is also involved in the development of EB612, a tablet peptide replacement therapy, which is in Phase I clinical trial for the treatment of hypoparathyroidism; EB618, a GLP-1/glucagon dual agonist peptide, which is in Phase I clinical trial for the treatment of obesity, metabolic, and fibrotic disorders; and GLP-2 which is in Phase I clinical trial for the treatment of short bowel syndrome and disorders related to mucosal inflammation and nutrient malabsorption. It has a collaboration agreement with OPKO Biologics, Inc for the preclinical and clinical development of LA-PTH and oral dual agonist GLP-1/glucagon peptide. The company was incorporated in 2009 and is based in Jerusalem, Israel.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Miranda J. Toledano M.B.A. | CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $562,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 27 people. Revenue per employee of $2K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 48%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $102K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 361\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Entera Bio Ltd. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $542M market cap on $42,000 of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -58% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -192% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 15% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $7M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 1.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 6548% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 5.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 27450% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 60/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 204% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Entera Bio (NASDAQ:ENTX) Releases Quarterly Earnings Results, Misses Expectations By $0.05 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/entera-bio-nasdaqentx-releases-quarterly-earnings-results-misses-expectations-by-0-05-eps.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794094965.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Entera Bio GAAP EPS of -$0.11 misses by $0.04 (NASDAQ:ENTX)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668619-entera-bio-gaap-eps-of-0_11-misses-by-0_04","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000303.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.66,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Head-To-Head Review: OSR (NASDAQ:OSRH) and Entera Bio (NASDAQ:ENTX)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https